# Vercel Web Analytics Configuration Update

## Summary
Updated the Vercel Web Analytics implementation to use the latest official documentation standards for Next.js App Router projects.

## Changes Made

### Modified Files
- **src/app/layout.js** - Updated Analytics component import path

### What Was Done

1. **Fetched Latest Documentation**: Retrieved the official Vercel Analytics quickstart guide from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart to ensure the most up-to-date implementation approach.

2. **Updated Import Path**: Changed the Analytics import from `@vercel/analytics/react` to `@vercel/analytics/next` as specified in the latest Next.js App Router documentation. This is the recommended import path for Next.js projects using the App Router.

3. **Verified Installation**: Confirmed that `@vercel/analytics` package (version 1.4.1) was already installed in package.json.

4. **Installed Dependencies**: Ran `npm install` to ensure all dependencies are properly installed and lock files are updated.

5. **Verified Implementation**: 
   - Confirmed the Analytics component is correctly placed in the root layout file
   - Verified the component is positioned inside the `<body>` tag as per documentation
   - Checked that the package exports the correct module at `@vercel/analytics/next`
   - Ran linter to ensure no code quality issues were introduced

## Implementation Details

The Analytics component is now imported using the framework-specific path for Next.js:
```javascript
import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";
```

This import provides optimized analytics tracking for Next.js applications with proper support for:
- Server-side rendering (SSR)
- Client-side navigation
- App Router architecture
- Automatic page view tracking

The `<Analytics />` component is correctly positioned at the end of the `<body>` tag in the root layout, which ensures it loads after the main content and tracks all page views across the application.

## Notes

- The project uses Next.js App Router architecture with the layout file at `src/app/layout.js`
- The Analytics component requires no additional configuration or environment variables for basic functionality
- Analytics will automatically activate when the application is deployed to Vercel
- To view analytics data, enable Analytics in the Vercel dashboard for this project

## Build Status

- Dependencies: ✅ Installed successfully
- Linter: ✅ No errors introduced
- Build: ⚠️ Project has pre-existing Firebase configuration issue (invalid API key) unrelated to this change
